## HANDOUT 1.2.A: Celsius-Fahrenheit Conversion

1. The following table shows pairs of equivalent temperatures measured using two different scales, Celsius and Fahrenheit. Use the patterns in the table to fill in three more rows that show a temperature in degrees Celsius and its equivalent temperature in degrees Fahrenheit.

| °C | °F |
| :---: | :---: |
| 0 | 32 |
| 5 | 41 |
| 10 | 50 |
| 15 | 59 |
| 20 | 68 |
| 25 | 77 |
| 30 | 86 |
| 35 | 95 |
| 40 | 104 |
| | |
| | |
| | |

2. Is the relationship between the two temperature scales in the table linear? Is it proportional? Explain your reasoning.

3. Graph the data in the table and then write an equation where the input is a temperature in degrees Celsius and the output is a temperature in degrees Fahrenheit.

